{#
  One member on the Membership page. Expects a `person` variable (an item from
  `collections.members`).

  Deliberately quieter than the Executive Board card: photo, name, title,
  nothing to open and no panel around it. Officers get a bio because the
  membership needs to know who is accountable; a member entry is a roll call,
  so it is three lines under a face and nothing more.

  Same empty-photo fallback as everywhere else — a missing headshot shows the
  neutral avatar rather than a broken image or a hole in the grid.

  The name becomes a link only when `link` is filled in. An empty field leaves
  plain text rather than an anchor pointing at the current page, so nobody
  clicks a name and stays exactly where they were.
#}

<article class="member">
  {% if person.data.photo %}
    <img
      class="member__photo"
      src="{{ person.data.photo }}"
      alt="{{ person.data.name }}"
      width="84"
      height="84"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  {% else %}
    <span class="member__photo member__photo--empty" role="img"
          aria-label="{{ labels.noPhotoPrefix }} {{ person.data.name }}">
      {% include "partials/avatar-icon.njk" %}
    </span>
  {% endif %}

  <h3 class="member__name">
    {% if person.data.link %}
      <a href="{{ person.data.link }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ person.data.name }}</a>
    {% else %}
      {{ person.data.name }}
    {% endif %}
  </h3>
  {% if person.data.title %}
    <p class="member__title">{{ person.data.title }}</p>
  {% endif %}
</article>
